            "diagnosis_background.1"
          ],
          "text": "Primary: Bronchiolitis (clinical diagnosis, RSV season); RSV positive on nasopharyngeal aspirate.\n\nBackground: Born at term with no significant past medical history; immunisations up to date. No family history of atopy noted.",
          "unverified_fact_ids": []
        },
        {
          "section_id": "sections.2",
          "part": "part_a",
          "heading": "key_investigations",
          "fact_ids": [
            "key_investigations.0",
            "key_investigations.1",
            "key_investigations.2",
            "key_investigations.3"
          ],
          "text": "On admission: temperature 37.6, respiratory rate 58, mild-moderate subcostal recession, widespread fine creps and wheeze, oxygen saturations 90% on room air. Nasopharyngeal aspirate (NPA) sent and returned RSV positive.\n\nDay 2: oxygen saturations 93–95% on room air after weaning off oxygen; respiratory rate 44, mild recession only; feeding improving to approximately 75% orally.",
          "unverified_fact_ids": []
        },
        {
          "section_id": "sections.3",
          "part": "part_a",
          "heading": "treatment",
          "fact_ids": [
            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3",
            "treatment.4"
          ],
          "text": "Supportive care was provided with supplemental oxygen to maintain saturations ≥90%. Nasogastric feeds were commenced (with IV fluids as contingency if not tolerated). No antibiotics were given given the viral aetiology. Salbutamol was not given (not indicated in bronchiolitis). The nasogastric tube was removed on Day 2 when the infant was tolerating approximately 75% oral feeds.",
          "unverified_fact_ids": []
        },
